#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:1
msgid "pretty-bytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:3
msgid "Convert bytes to a human readable string: `1337` → `1.34 kB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:5
msgid "Useful for displaying file sizes for humans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:7
msgid ""
"*Note that it uses base-10 (e.g. kilobyte). [Read about the difference "
"between kilobyte and "
"kibibyte.](https://web.archive.org/web/20150324153922/https://pacoup.com/2009/05/26"
"/kb-kb-kib-whats-up-with-that/)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:10
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:16
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:40
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:42
msgid "prettyBytes(number, options?)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:44
msgid "number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:46
msgid "Type: `number`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:48
msgid "The number to format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:50
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:52
msgid "Type: `object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:54
msgid "signed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:56
#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:63
#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:70
msgid "Type: `boolean` Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:59
msgid ""
"Include plus sign for positive numbers. If the difference is exactly zero"
" a space character will be prepended instead for better alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:61
msgid "bits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:66
msgid ""
"Format the number as [bits](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit) instead of"
" [bytes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byte). This can be useful when, "
"for example, referring to [bit "
"rate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit_rate)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:68
msgid "binary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:73
msgid ""
"Format the number using the [Binary "
"Prefix](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binary_prefix) instead of the [SI "
"Prefix](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SI_prefix). This can be useful for "
"presenting memory amounts. However, this should not be used for "
"presenting file sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:75
msgid "locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:77
msgid "Type: `boolean | string` Default: `false` *(No localization)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:80
msgid ""
"**Important:** Only the number and decimal separator are localized. The "
"unit title is not and will not be localized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:82
msgid "If `true`: Localize the output using the system/browser locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:83
msgid ""
"If `string`: Expects a [BCP 47 language "
"tag](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IETF_language_tag) (For example: `en`,"
" `de`, …)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:84
msgid ""
"If `string[]`: Expects a list of [BCP 47 language "
"tags](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IETF_language_tag) (For example: "
"`en`, `de`, …)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:86
msgid ""
"**Note:** Localization should generally work in browsers. Node.js needs "
"to be [built](https://github.com/nodejs/node/wiki/Intl) with `full-icu` "
"or `system-icu`. Alternatively, the [`full-icu`](https://github.com"
"/unicode-org/full-icu-npm) module can be used to provide support at "
"runtime. [Node.js 13](https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v13.0.0/) and "
"later ships with ICU by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:88
msgid "minimumFractionDigits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:90
#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:110
msgid "Type: `number` Default: `undefined`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:93
msgid "The minimum number of fraction digits to display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:95
#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:115
msgid ""
"If neither `minimumFractionDigits` or `maximumFractionDigits` are set, "
"the default behavior is to round to 3 significant digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:108
msgid "maximumFractionDigits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pretty-bytes_readme.md:113
msgid "The maximum number of fraction digits to display."
msgstr ""

